BT /F1 10 Tf 50 770 Td (# Launch Guide for Movies & Politics) Tj T* () Tj T* (## Overview) Tj T* (This guide explains how to:) Tj T* (- preview the site locally,) Tj T* (- update movie and political content,) Tj T* (- add your mobile and email contact information,) Tj T* (- build the app for production,) Tj T* (- deploy it to the web.) Tj T* () Tj T* (## 1. Local setup and preview) Tj T* (1. Open a terminal in the project root: `c:\\Users\\venka\\New folder`) Tj T* (2. Install dependencies if not already installed:) Tj T* (   - `npm install`) Tj T* (3. Start the local development server:) Tj T* (   - `npm run dev`) Tj T* (4. Open the app in your browser:) Tj T* (   - `http://localhost:5173/`) Tj T* () Tj T* (## 2. Link your mobile number and email) Tj T* (The footer already has a contact section using `tel:` and `mailto:` links.) Tj T* () Tj T* (To set your real details:) Tj T* (1. Open `src/App.jsx`.) Tj T* (2. Find the `CONTACT` constant near the top of the file.) Tj T* (3. Replace the placeholders with your actual phone number and email address:) Tj T* (   ```js) Tj T* (   const CONTACT = {) Tj T* (     phone: '+91-12345-67890',) Tj T* (     email: 'you@example.com') Tj T* (   };) Tj T* (   ```) Tj T* (4. Save the file and refresh the browser.) Tj T* () Tj T* (## 3. How to add news and updates) Tj T* (### Movies) Tj T* (Movie updates are defined in the `movies` array inside `src/App.jsx`.) Tj T* (Each item includes fields such as:) Tj T* (- `title`) Tj T* (- `release`) Tj T* (- `category`) Tj T* (- `genre`) Tj T* (- `status`) Tj T* (- `reportType`) Tj T* (- `platform`) Tj T* (- `cast`) Tj T* (- `director`) Tj T* (- `rating`) Tj T* (- `description`) Tj T* (- `image`) Tj T* () Tj T* (To add a new movie update:) Tj T* (1. Open `src/App.jsx`.) Tj T* (2. Add a new object to the `movies` array.) Tj T* (3. Provide both English and Telugu text when available using fields like `title_te`, `description_te`, etc.) Tj T* (4. Save the file and refresh the site.) Tj T* () Tj T* (### Political news) Tj T* (Political items are defined in the `politicalNews` array in `src/App.jsx`.) Tj T* (The app now supports the following political filters:) Tj T* (- `All updates`) Tj T* (- `International`) Tj T* (- `National`) Tj T* (- `Telangana`) Tj T* (- `Andhra Pradesh`) Tj T* () Tj T* (To add a political update:) Tj T* (1. Open `src/App.jsx`.) Tj T* (2. Add a new object to the `politicalNews` array.) Tj T* (3. Set the `category` field to one of the supported sections above.) Tj T* (4. Save the file and refresh.) Tj T* () Tj T* (### Local news) Tj T* (Local items are defined in the `localNews` array.) Tj T* (Add any community or neighborhood story there.) Tj T* () Tj T* (## 4. How the site displays updates) Tj T* (### Movie section) Tj T* (- The main movie tab now starts with `New updates`.) Tj T* (- Movies can also appear in `Tollywood` or `Box Office India` views based on the `industry` and `category` fields.) Tj T* (- The `Latest updates` tab surfaces upcoming or recently released titles.) Tj T* () Tj T* (### Political section) Tj T* (- A common news list shows all political headlines first.) Tj T* (- A separate filtered section displays stories for the selected political category.) Tj T* (- Each news item should use one of the categories: `International`, `National`, `Telangana`, or `Andhra Pradesh`.) Tj T* () Tj T* (## 5. Build for production) Tj T* (1. In the project root, run:) Tj T* (   - `npm run build`) Tj T* (2. The production-ready files will be generated in the `dist/` folder.) Tj T* (3. Preview the build locally with:) Tj T* (   - `npm run preview`) Tj T* (4. Open the preview URL shown in the terminal.) Tj T* () Tj T* (## 6. Deploying to the web) Tj T* (### Option 1: Netlify) Tj T* (1. Sign up at https://www.netlify.com) Tj T* (2. Connect your GitHub repository or drag the `dist/` folder into Netlify.) Tj T* (3. Set the build command to `npm run build` and publish directory to `dist`.) Tj T* (4. Deploy and use the generated Netlify URL.) Tj T* () Tj T* (### Option 2: Vercel) Tj T* (1. Sign up at https://vercel.com) Tj T* (2. Import the project from GitHub.) Tj T* (3. Use `npm install` as install command and `npm run build` as build command.) Tj T* (4. Deploy and use the Vercel URL.) Tj T* () Tj T* (### Option 3: GitHub Pages) Tj T* (1. Build the app with `npm run build`.) Tj T* (2. Use a GitHub Pages deploy action or copy the `dist/` contents to the `gh-pages` branch.) Tj T* (3. Serve the built site from GitHub Pages.) Tj T* () Tj T* (### Custom domain) Tj T* (1. After deployment, point your domain to the host provider.) Tj T* (2. For Netlify, add the domain in site settings and update DNS records.) Tj T* (3. For Vercel, add the custom domain and verify ownership.) Tj T* () Tj T* (## 7. Updating the site for audience reflection) Tj T* (- For now, the app is a static React site. That means content changes require editing `src/App.jsx` and redeploying.) Tj T* (- After each content update, run `npm run build` and redeploy the `dist/` folder.) Tj T* (- If you want live updating without rebuilding, the next step is to connect a backend API or CMS.) Tj T* () Tj T* (## 8. Quick checklist) Tj T* (- [ ] Replace `CONTACT` values in `src/App.jsx`.) Tj T* (- [ ] Add movie updates in the `movies` array.) Tj T* (- [ ] Add political updates in the `politicalNews` array with the correct category.) Tj T* (- [ ] Add local updates in the `localNews` array.) Tj T* (- [ ] Run `npm run build` to verify.) Tj T* (- [ ] Deploy the `dist/` folder to Netlify, Vercel, or GitHub Pages.) Tj T* () Tj T* (## 9. Note on future automation) Tj T* (If you want updates to appear automatically for all users without manual rebuilds, consider:) Tj T* (- adding a backend database,) Tj T* (- exposing an API for news items,) Tj T* (- storing updates in JSON or a headless CMS,) Tj T* (- fetching live news via API keys.) Tj T* () Tj T* (---) Tj T* () Tj T* (This guide is designed to provide a complete local and web launch process for the Movies & Politics site.) Tj T* () Tj ET
endstream
